4.2 Widget classification The maker shall assign a widget class to each widget. The assignment shall consider:
a) the worst credible consequence of a fault;
b) the measures outside the widget that limit that consequence;
c) the intended environment of use. The maker shall record the rationale for the assigned class. [Class A, B]
NOTE 1 Class A widgets cannot contribute to an unsafe condition. Class B widgets can.
NOTE 2 The class can change after a modification; see 5.2.

